# One line-ending policy on every platform: LF in the repository and in every
# checkout. Rendered SQL is compared and checksummed byte-for-byte (CLAUDE.md
# §7.23; "byte-identical to the C# reference", php/CODING-STANDARD.md §5), and
# the DDL literals that produce it — C# raw strings, PHP nowdocs — carry the
# source file's physical newlines. A CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows, or a `git archive` taken from one) therefore changes migration
# checksums and fails SqliteDialectTest::version_table_sql_matches_the_reference_ddl;
# php/bin/simpleorm is a shell script whose shebang line must end in LF.
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf; `text=auto` keeps any future binary out.
* text=auto eol=lf
